WEBVTT


00:00:00.690 --> 00:00:06.270
The newest additions to the Knit it
Now Basics patterns are sideways knits.

00:00:07.490 --> 00:00:13.730
These styles are a refreshing change of
pace from your traditional hem to neck

00:00:13.880 --> 00:00:18.170
knitting patterns, and they
offer new design possibilities.

00:00:28.065 --> 00:00:30.615
The pieces are started at the arm hole.

00:00:31.545 --> 00:00:35.535
For a sleeveless version,
you cast on and hang hem.

00:00:36.855 --> 00:00:40.265
If you want sleeves,
cast on with waste yarn.

00:00:42.945 --> 00:00:49.215
Next you'll work the side seams, shaped
or straight, whichever you prefer.

00:00:53.135 --> 00:00:58.325
Lengthening and shortening this sweater
is a matter of adding or removing needles

00:01:00.605 --> 00:01:03.725
because the sweater is
kn it from side to side.

00:01:04.115 --> 00:01:09.665
Any horizontal stitch patterns
becomes slimming vertical details.

00:01:10.835 --> 00:01:14.555
You can even add stripes for
more casual look to your sweater.

00:01:16.425 --> 00:01:18.735
Pull over neck lines are simplified.

00:01:19.515 --> 00:01:24.495
Unlike traditional sweater shapes, you
don't have to work the two sides of the

00:01:24.495 --> 00:01:26.055
neck opening separately

00:01:28.595 --> 00:01:33.365
and for cardigans, you don't have to
pick up and rehang the front bands.

00:01:33.725 --> 00:01:38.525
Simply hang a hem and work button
holes to finish the center front.

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:46.160
To add sleeves, you would cast on at
your arm holes with waste yarn, knit your

00:01:46.160 --> 00:01:47.570
fronts and backs.

00:01:48.410 --> 00:01:53.480
Then join the shoulders, pick up your
sleeves and knit them down to the cuffs.

00:01:55.070 --> 00:01:59.660
You can work some ribbing, hang a
hem and your sleeves are finished.

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:06.450
The hem of this sweater style
offers lots of possibilities.

00:02:08.445 --> 00:02:11.865
One option is to simply
finish the hems with crochet.

00:02:12.315 --> 00:02:13.875
But think about this.

00:02:14.235 --> 00:02:21.465
Leave a needle out of work about an
inch or so in and create a fold line.

00:02:22.545 --> 00:02:28.035
When your sweater's complete and you've
sewn up your side seams, simply fold up

00:02:28.035 --> 00:02:31.155
the hem along this line
and stitch it in place.

00:02:34.810 --> 00:02:36.700
You can pick up and knit some ribbing.

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:42.859
Another option is to add a peplum
to the bottom of the sweater.

00:02:46.730 --> 00:02:51.540
You can also hang a band, just
a regular band on the hems.

00:02:52.305 --> 00:03:00.195
We offer fitted versions of this sweater
with a four inch bottom band, and we also

00:03:00.195 --> 00:03:03.045
have a no waist shaping
version of this sweater.

00:03:03.045 --> 00:03:04.995
With the smaller hem,

00:03:07.335 --> 00:03:09.165
are you starting to get inspired?

00:03:10.095 --> 00:03:14.595
Consider a Basics sideways knit
sweater for your next project.

